## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

**Summary: 10 tests, 9 Critical findings, 1 Medium.** This suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** pattern — every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called (giving ~95% coverage) but almost nothing is actually verified.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Tests giving false confidence

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic)
**Lines 16–89 · All 10 tests**

The test class methodically calls every public member on `ProductCatalog` in declaration order. 6 of 10 tests have **zero assertions**; the remaining 4 assert only `IsNotNull` — a trivial check that proves nothing about correctness. This is exactly why bugs reach production despite 95% coverage.

---

#### 2. No Assertions (6 tests)

| Test | Line | What's untested |
|------|------|-----------------|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17 | Never checks the product was actually stored |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 32 | Never checks the price changed to 14.99 |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 38 | Never checks the product was deleted |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 63 | Never checks the count value (not even `IsNotNull`) |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 68 | Never checks prices were reduced by 10% |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85 | Never checks a product was created from the CSV |

**Fix for each** — add assertions that verify the *outcome*:

```csharp
// AddProduct_Works → verify the product is retrievable
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored?.Price);
}

// UpdatePrice_Works → verify the price actually changed
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesProductPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
}

// RemoveProduct_Works → verify the product is gone
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_DeletesProduct()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}

// GetProductCount_Works → verify the count value
[TestMethod]
public void GetProductCount_ReturnsCorrectCount()
{
    Assert.AreEqual(0, _catalog.GetProductCount());
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
}

// ApplyBulkDiscount_Works → verify prices reduced
[TestMethod]
